  ~
  ~ Persian. Replaces the upstream values-fa-rIR file, for two reasons.
  ~
  ~ First, coverage: 167 of the app's 373 strings — effectively the whole Portway surface, from
  ~ onboarding to the home screen to the update prompt — had no Persian at all and were falling
  ~ back to English mid-sentence. A large share of this app's users read Persian.
  ~
  ~ Second, the qualifier: "fa-rIR" only matches Iran. Persian speakers in Afghanistan (fa-AF)
  ~ and anyone whose device reports a bare "fa" fell through to English for the entire app. This
  ~ file is qualified on the language alone, so it matches all of them.
  ~
  ~ Register: the audience is people handed a config by a provider, so the words they already use
  ~ win over purist coinages — کانفیگ, پینگ, هندشیک, سرور. Field names that appear verbatim in a
  ~ .conf file stay recognisable, because a user comparing the screen with the file they were sent
  ~ has to be able to match them line for line. Numerals stay Latin throughout: these screens
  ~ carry IP addresses, ports, MTUs and base64 keys.
  -->
